1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,963
What's inside ApplicationContext?

2
00:00:02,083 --> 00:00:04,500
Bean definitions are recipes.

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,160
Managed instances

4
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,376
are the actual objects.

5
00:00:07,556 --> 00:00:09,420
Register configuration,

6
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:10,800
then refresh.

7
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,020
Spring reads the definitions

8
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:14,797
and creates our singleton beans.

9
00:00:14,977 --> 00:00:16,880
Calling getBean returns the service,

10
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:19,861
already wired to its repository.

11
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:22,480
The context also publishes events.

12
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:22,920
Close it,

13
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,956
and managed cleanup runs.

14
00:00:25,136 --> 00:00:27,040
Our tests confirm: same service,

15
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,580
one event, cleanup called.

16
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:30,020
Definitions describe;

17
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:32,276
instances do the work.

18
00:00:34,276 --> 00:00:35,462
Thanks for watching.

